{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79QaYmXmauoktXU6sej","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've apologized directly for the lack of refunds and the one short email. Those are the likeliest reasons people left. I didn't promise that the farm is now protected from hail, because the nets only cover tomatoes and peppers. The draft is about 165 words. Fill in the name, farm and link placeholders before sending.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: We let you down last summer. Here's what we've changed.\n\nHi [First name],\n\nYou didn't renew your farm share last year, and I understand why. The July 9 hailstorm destroyed about half our crops. For six weeks after that, your boxes had only about half the usual amount. We didn't offer refunds or credit, and I sent you just one short email about it. You deserved better than that, and I'm sorry.\n\nHere's what we've changed since then:\n\n- **A second field on higher ground**, so our crops aren't all in one place.\n- **Two hail nets** over our tomatoes and peppers.\n- **Pauses with credit.** You can now pause your share for up to 2 weeks and get credit for those weeks.\n\nThese changes cost us $31,000, but a full share is still $540, the same as last year.\n\nSign-up closes March 15, and there are 52 shares left. If you'd like to come back, you can sign up here: [link]\n\nIf you have thoughts on how we handled last season, please just reply to this email. I'd really like to hear them.\n\n[Your name]\n[Farm name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5408,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5408},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nul